schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-RFINISH
wu: E-RFINISH.W3
branch: wu/redesign-finish/perf-bench
tests:
  unit:
    count: 16
    covers: "xtask/src/ui.rs (1) - `ui bench` takes no arguments and is listed in USAGE. TimestampText.test.tsx (3) - today's bounds and the year's bounds are exact to the millisecond either side, and a timestamp is re-labelled once the clock leaves the day it was rendered under, which is the memo's generation asserted through the rendered string rather than through a private helper. flow.test.ts (5) - hostOf returns exactly what a full new URL() parse returns across port, default port, userinfo, IPv6, punycode, query-terminated and slash-less authorities; agrees with toRow on all of them; names no host for a URI that has none; is stable across repeats; and keeps answering correctly past its own memo bound. body.test.ts (5) - decodeBody reports a whole decode; reports one whole even where the body carries a replacement character of its own (the case a downstream scan cannot tell from damage); reports a lossy one and still returns text to render; calls a byte-order-marked body whole though the mark leaves its text, so the body's size stays its bytes'; and calls an empty body whole. TextRenderer.test.tsx (2) - states the size its caller already knew, and derives a byte-identical string where the caller cannot supply one."
  integration:
    count: 6
    covers: "ui/src/perf.test.tsx - the WU contract at each seam, asserted as work not done paired with the output that must not move, plus two regression tests for a defect this WU's own review found in it. (1) FlowList re-rendered ten times parses no timestamp and its time cells stay string-identical; (2) a useFlows refresh whose hosts are already known parses no URI, observed by replacing globalThis.URL with a counting subclass across a real debounced refresh, and the host list is identical by reference; (3) TextRenderer and (4) BodyViewer never hand the untruncated body to TextEncoder, cut marker asserted as a literal; (5) REGRESSION - a text/*-labelled body that will not decode states no shown size larger than its total, the inverted statement the first review round found; (6) REGRESSION - a whole body that carries a replacement character of its own keeps the free size rather than being read as damaged, the false positive the second round found in the first fix. Tests 1-4 were run against the pre-fix tree and all four fail there (640 stray moment parses, 40 stray URI parses, a 136072-character encode in each body case); 5 and 6 were each run against the version they guard and fail there. Deterministic and hermetic: call counts and rendered strings, no timing assertion at any level."
  e2e:
    waived: "No contract moves - all three costs are cost, not behaviour, and the rendered output is identical everywhere the suite can see it. The only difference an e2e could observe is a duration, which the testing standard forbids asserting at every level. The epic's e2e is W10 and covers no part of this WU. The measurement that does exist is the committed benchmark (cargo xtask ui bench), deliberately outside the suite and outside every gate because wall-clock numbers are not deterministic; the six integration tests are what the gate reads instead."
